\pard\sb260\sa100\keepn\fs32\cf1\b A. Application Overview\b0\cf0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 The Secure Student Club Registration and Membership Management System replaces informal club sign-up with a web workflow. Students register, sign in, browse clubs, submit membership applications, and view pending, approved, or rejected decisions. Club administrators review applications, approve or reject pending requests, create and edit club listings, set member capacity, and view approved members.\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 The two roles are Student and Club Administrator. Students can browse clubs and access only their own applications. Administrators can review requests and maintain club information. Express checks authorization on the server for each restricted API route.\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Technologies: Node.js, Express, SQLite, HTML, CSS, browser JavaScript, bcryptjs, express-session with a SQLite store, Node crypto (AES-256-GCM and HMAC), Zod, Helmet, express-rate-limit, and Winston.\par
\pard\sb260\sa100\keepn\fs32\cf1\b Main features 2\b0\cf0\fs20\par
\pard\li360\fi-220\sa65\fs20\cf0\bullet\tab Student registration, login, logout, club browsing, membership applications, and status tracking.\par
\pard\li360\fi-220\sa65\fs20\cf0\bullet\tab Administrator review of applications, club creation and editing, member capacity settings, and approved-member list.\par
\pard\li360\fi-220\sa65\fs20\cf0\bullet\tab Encrypted student identity fields, server-side role checks, validated inputs, CSRF protection, secure session configuration, and structured security logs.\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Scope note: profile editing, password reset, email verification, per-club administrator assignment, automated backups, and production deployment are not implemented in this version.\par
\pard\sb260\sa100\keepn\fs32\cf1\b Cyber flow 2\b0\cf0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Browser -> Helmet and Express middleware -> session and CSRF checks -> Zod validation -> role authorization -> parameterized SQLite operation -> AES-GCM decryption only for an authorized admin response -> JSON response -> escaped browser rendering. Winston records important events. Registration hashes passwords with bcrypt and encrypts student PII before storage. Login compares the bcrypt hash and rotates the session ID.\par
\pard\sb260\sa100\keepn\fs32\cf1\b Run configuration 2\b0\cf0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Install dependencies with npm install, keep .env private, and start with npm start. On the same computer, open http://127.0.0.1:3000. The health endpoint is http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/health. Local development uses HTTP and is not HTTPS evidence.\par
