\pard\sb260\sa100\keepn\fs32\cf1\b D. Challenges and Solutions\b0\cf0\fs20\par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa75\fs18\cf0\b Server startup failed because SESSION_SECRET was missing/short. The server showed a configuration validation error. A long secret was added to the project .env file.\b0  \par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa75\fs18\cf0\b DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY was still the example placeholder and had invalid length. The server rejected it at startup. A fresh 32-byte random key was generated and saved privately in .env.\b0  \par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa75\fs18\cf0\b TLS path contained a value that was not a certificate file. Invalid TLS paths were cleared for local HTTP; HTTPS needs actual key and certificate files.\b0  \par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa75\fs18\cf0\b The login page was reported unavailable although the service started. The health endpoint later returned 200, proving only API reachability. Browser login flow remains to be verified on your local browser.\b0  \par
\pard\li180\ri180\sa75\fs18\cf0\b PowerShell showed a script parsing warning on the health check. The request still returned 200. -UseBasicParsing suppresses this legacy PowerShell warning.\b0  \par
\pard\sb260\sa100\keepn\fs32\cf1\b E. Security Summary\b0\cf0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Confidentiality: bcrypt password hashes, AES-GCM selected identity fields, keyed HMAC lookup, and RBAC restrict access. HTTPS is required in deployment but is not active in the local run.\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Integrity: server validation, prepared SQL, CSRF tokens, role authorization, unique application constraint, pending-only decisions, capacity checks, and audit logs protect records and decisions.\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Availability: request-size limits, login rate limits, persistent SQLite storage, and safe error handling support reliable operation. Backups, monitoring, multi-instance storage, and recovery plans are not configured.\par
