\pard\sb260\sa100\keepn\fs32\cf1\b Viva Preparation 2\b0\cf0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100\sl260\slmult1\fs20\cf0 Why bcrypt? It makes password guessing expensive and stores no plaintext password. Why AES-GCM? It encrypts selected PII and authenticates ciphertext against tampering. Why enforce roles on the API? Client controls can be bypassed, so each protected request must check the session role. What does CSRF protection do? It requires a session-bound unpredictable token for state-changing requests. Is local transport HTTPS? No; the local project uses HTTP. What tests are complete? Syntax checks and the reported health check only; the remaining matrix still needs to be run.\par
